--TEST--
an attribute an interface declares is written by its short name on a class that implements it, and a jump from that name opens the `attribute` declaration inside the interface, `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
interface Page {
    attribute Path on method { path: string }

    public function render(): string;
}

class Home implements Page {
    #[Pa<|>th(path: "/")]
    public function render(): string { return "home"; }
}
--REQUEST--
definition
--EXPECT--
case.nvs:3:15
